Dealer, as a true businessperson, you need to make yourself presentable. So, what do you dress in, you ask? Well, let’s see!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43095044/e7cf465fd39cf74aa3e943a477b546185915294d.jpg[/img]
First of all, you gotta customise your character! And yes, you can already do that in the demo. You can change your shoes, pants, tops, hats, backpacks and jewellery. And they’re not just a decoration: your clothes do impact your stats.

[b]What stats get impacted by your great looks?[/b]
[list][*]Agility – impacts your overall mobility and performance of parkour;
[*]Visibility – impacts your visibility to others;
[*]Comfort – impacts the duration of status effects, both positive and negative;
[*]SWAG – helps in your negotiations and gaining more respect;
[*]SUS – affects how suspicious you look.[/list]
Some items of clothing can also add more storage slots and quickslots. And some clothes also add secret slots, which are handy when you get accosted by bandits trying to steal your stuff. All the items stashed in the secret slots are less likely to be discovered and taken away from you.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43095044/6f90f7200c1f0896bd584c8b90c81964974542fa.jpg[/img]
To buy new clothes simply visit the clothes shop. To change, interact with a wardrobe in your hideout or with the changing room in the shop.

